# rm317, the riddle of the cover (Docs/Design/84). Exported from ridgemere3 at revision 1: edit it in Atlas or the DM, or as a draft through tools/mantle_load.py.
mantle rm317
revision 1
state ready
dialect plain
accent broad light
tier standard
written_for rm_mab_coalridge
written_by codex
title the riddle of the cover
fits stage=adult|old
prefers job=servant honesty=guarded
traits temper=nervy talk=plain warmth=cold humour=none honesty=guarded piety=ordinary drive=steady
quirk turns_serving_covers_and_asks_what_they_keep_in
likes fried_fish riddles quiet_chapel misty_dawns
dislikes night_noise haggling
fears an_answer_given_in_the_wrong_room
hopes a_dry_cabin_with_a_closing_door
topics work +0.5 pastimes +0.5 food +0.4 gossip -0.6
styles comfort=shelter gossip=sealed refuse=cool tease=none
marks oath saying
persona #self.first# turns a serving cover over to catch its last drops and devises riddles about what a lid will keep out and what it ought to let go.

words
oath! = Loose pot ears | Three rattling covers
saying! = The lid keeps its own counsel | A clean drop needs no witness
lid = the shallow cover | my turned lid
drip = a clear drop | a little bead
lip = the rolled rim | the folded lip
pan = a low pan | a shallow dish
butter = the yellow butter | a dab of butter
fish = a crisp fish tail | the folded fillet
hinge = a little loop | the loose ring
mist = a strip of mist | the grey dawn veil
cot = a narrow cot | a dry bunk
blanket = my folded blanket | the warm cover
towel = a clean wiping cloth | a striped rag
closh = a tin dome | the hollow cover

any
opinion @1 houses against 1 : Ask what's under a rich cover and see how quickly a servant's voice becomes unwelcome.
opinion @1 church for 1 : A chapel that doesn't demand my whole history is somewhere I can rest.
opinion @1 merchants against 1 : I won't pay for food whose good smell is doing most of the work.
opinion @1 watch against 1 : Suspicion has a respectable jacket on when it walks beside a uniform. Still suspicion.
opinion @1 times against 1 : Even when the same dishes go out, the portions on them seem to keep shrinking.
opinion @1 sump for 1 : The low streets understand the difference between a door closed for warmth and a door closed for spite.

grown
line @1 greet : I've a moment while the lid cools. Hello. | Stand clear of the dripping edge. Welcome.
line @2 greet [pair.band=strangers] : I don't recognise that voice yet. | Hello. We can speak here in the open.
line @3 greet [here.time=dawn] : Morning. Steam hangs about before the air warms. | A quiet early word is welcome.
line @1 greet.return : I heard. I'm drying my paws first. | Hello to you. The drop's fallen now.
line @2 greet.return [pair.band=friends|family] : A familiar voice through all the clatter. | I know you well enough to sit a moment.
line @3 greet.return [here.time=night] : Late words carry far. I'll keep mine low. | Hello. The night's quiet enough to hear through tin.
line @1 again.open : We've met twice without the lid going cold. | Here again while there's a little warmth left.
line @1 hail [pair.band=friends] : Come hear what that loose ring's doing. | Over here beside the quiet part.
line @1 farewell : Keep well covered on the way. | Safe out and dry home.
line @1 farewell.return : I'll tip the last drop away and follow presently. | A little quiet on your journey.
line @1 react.news : Tell me only the part that's yours to tell. | I shall keep still while you explain.
line @1 react.news.new : No trace of that had reached this room. | That's entirely new to my hearing.
line @1 react.news.known : I know the matter. Your version is close. | Yes. I've heard that lid lifted already.
line @1 react.news.doubt : That seems a confident account of a covered dish. | I'd want more than a convincing smell.
line @1 react.news.sorrow [topic.kind=death|crime|assault|loss|theft] : I won't make a noise over it. Sit here as long as needed. | A poor end to a hard matter. I'll listen.
line @1 react.news.glad [topic.kind=marriage|birth|apprentice|work] : That's a welcome reason to lift the cover. | I could set out a clean plate to honour news like that.
line @1 ask.how : Any chance to sit away from the noise today? | How have you stood the heat?
line @1 answer.how : Quite able to work. A shade more tired than I sound. | Steady, so long as nobody rattles things.
line @1 decline : I'm too closely involved to give you an idle answer. | I intend to preserve a confidence that hasn't been returned to me.
line @1 accept_decline : I'll leave that question where it is. | You weren't obliged to let me in.
line @1 preclose : The work will cool if I leave it longer. | I've a quiet errand coming due.
line @1 accept_preclose : Go while there's a little space to move. | I can take care of the remaining drops.
line @1 thank : You've prevented quite an unnecessary fuss. Thanks. | That was a quiet kindness. I did notice.
line @1 deflect_thanks : A cloth was within reach already. | There wasn't a need for two of us to get splashed.
line @1 sympathise : You're welcome to sit without carrying on a conversation. | Quiet does a little good when words have done enough.
line @1 reassure : Let the worst of the steam clear first. | It's a little easier once you can see the rim.
line @1 ack : I can follow that without guessing. | I heard the small distinction there.
line @1 give.advice : Tilt a cover away from the waiting dish. | Speak when you know what room you're in.
scene turnriddle
when topic=work self.job=servant
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : What gathers supper without ever tasting the salt? | On the top it's dry. On the bottom it's all broth.
b : A hungry serving cloth? | Some sort of dish?
a : The lid. Steam condenses there and falls back wholly unseasoned. | A cover seen from below. The droplets are clear, whatever's in the pot.

scene dripaim
when topic=work self.job=servant self.working=yes
does warn / react.self / assess
a : Hold the rim over the pot another moment. | Turn the cover away from the plate.
b : Does that one drop matter? | It looks dry from here.
a : To a crisp piece of fish, yes. Best to keep the good surface as it is. | The wet side's underneath. That's the part I have in mind.

scene riddletime
when topic=pastimes self.likes=riddles
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : My favourite riddles yield their answer to a neatly inverted question. | Some riddles have a plain side and a polished one.
b : Which is the true answer? | An example, then?
a : Ask what holds a bowlful upside down. A cover does, a bowl would lose the lot. | What vessel travels empty on its belly and full on its back? My little lid in the wash pan.

scene butterfish
when topic=food self.likes=fried_fish
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : Fish done in butter deserves a short trip to the table. | I try to put the crisp side uppermost.
b : Does the underside suffer? | What if it has a cover?
a : A little. An upper surface gives its steam somewhere to go. | Lift it promptly. A whole good crust can disappear in its own damp.

scene quietdoors
when topic=faith self.likes=quiet_chapel
does tell.feeling / react.self / assess
a : In chapel when it's quiet I listen for the moment the door stops moving. | A closing chapel door is a fine sound to me.
b : Why the door? | What happens after that?
a : Kitchen doors go on swinging. This one comes to rest. | A silence that isn't waiting for me to fill it with work.

scene mistdawn
when topic=weather here.weather=fog
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I quite like a morning when the roof edge disappears into mist. | Mist gives an ordinary sill a private little world.
b : Doesn't it make you uneasy? | What can you see from there?
a : Less than being plainly visible to everybody in the street. | A few drops, the sill, my own paws. Plenty for a short pause.

scene shifts
when topic=home self.quarter=works
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : In the Works the change of shift is plain from the pace of the feet. | My street has a different note going to work from coming home.
b : Which sound is quicker? | You listen to all that?
a : Going in. Coming home some feet have bags and aching backs to consider. | It's hard not to. I'm most interested in the interval between.

scene nonnoise
when topic=day here.time=night self.dislikes=night_noise
does tell.complaint / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : A lid dropped after dark seems to ring along every cupboard. | I want the little pot rings set flat at night.
b : Do they really make such a racket? | All neatly packed away?
a : One ring against tin, then another. It's like a whole table clearing its throat. | I'd settle for quiet. My eyes are generally shut at that hour.

scene nohaggle
when topic=prices self.dislikes=haggling
does give.opinion / react.self / assess
a : Say the price, let me choose, keep the dish covered in the meantime. | Bargaining over hot food does neither party much good.
b : What if the first price is high? | You'd leave it on the fire?
a : Then I'll go hungry a little longer. The fish won't improve while I argue. | Away from the heat, under a loose cover. I've a sensible limit to my patience.

scene parcel_sense
when topic=smalltalk
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : Wrapping can tell a great deal about a parcel without giving away what's inside. | A turned-in corner says whoever did the folding expected damp.
b : Do you guess the contents? | More than a label tells you?
a : Sometimes. I know enough to keep a guess in its proper place. | About the wrapping, certainly. The label is its own separate question.

scene dry_berth
when topic=dreams
does tell.plan / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : A dry sleeping place afloat appeals more than a grand cabin ashore. | I'd take a cabin small enough to touch both walls if the roof held.
b : Don't you mind the rocking? | And the closeness?
a : Rocking won't wet a blanket of its own accord. That's my main stipulation. | Less than a long cold drip on my ear. Small can be restful.

scene bad_faith
when topic=gossip
does give.opinion / react.self / assess
a : A crest on the cover doesn't vouch for anything inside. | Good manners can conceal a contrary purpose rather effectively.
b : You distrust all fine manners? | Would you look under the cover?
a : Not all. I simply keep their merits apart from the merits of the contents. | If it was my duty. Otherwise it could keep its mystery and its praise.

scene friend_gift
when topic=friends self.friend
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I'd put aside the driest crisp corner for #self.friend#. | I could share a plate with #self.friend# without explaining why I'm quiet.
b : Only a small share? | Would you make a visit of it?
a : Of the best bit, yes. There's more of the ordinary part to divide. | A meal together would do. No ceremony is needed to taste well-cooked fish.

scene heat_rag
when topic=work self.job=servant
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : A wet cloth can carry heat through to the paw unpleasantly quickly. | I keep a dry cloth separate from the cloth meant for wiping.
b : They look alike. | Which one are you reaching for?
a : They feel different. I make certain of the difference before lifting a warm dish. | The dry one if I'm lifting. I'd like my paws to see another day of work.

scene leanplate
when topic=times world.times=lean|hard
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : When food's scant I arrange a small helping so it won't go cold straight away. | What there is should arrive as well as it can.
b : Could a bigger cover help? | Trying to disguise the size?
a : A warm plate beats even a tremendous empty dome. | No. A small true portion is better than an elaborate disappointment.

scene shipview
when topic=ships here.region=ridgemere
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I'm content to admire a ship without naming its owner. | A boat seen from here is simply a place that may go elsewhere.
b : Is the owner a secret? | Do you want to go too?
a : I've no reason to suppose so. I just haven't inquired. | Sometimes. I'd enquire about the roof before the destination.

scene stormvoice
when topic=weather here.weather=storm
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : Thunder makes an iron kitchen seem a surprisingly small instrument. | A long roll outside puts my nuisance of a loose ring in its place.
b : Is that comforting? | D'you like a storm then?
a : In a sound room, yes. I prefer noise without an intention behind it. | Under cover, certainly. Much of my good temper depends on a sound roof.

scene festivaldoor
when topic=festival
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : At a feast I'm happiest just inside the service door. | A festival sounds better within reach of a quiet room.
b : Can you have any fun there? | Keeping away from the crowd?
a : I can hear the singing and still taste my supper. It suits me. | Keeping a choice. I can join in when the time is agreeable.

story fourthcalm [topic=memories|work self.job=servant]
  : I once lined three lids up, each wider than the one before. Tried them all and still had an uncovered pot.
  : The right lid was beneath it serving as a stand.
  b : Who put it there?
  : Me. I recognised the little bit of cloth I'd put under it to keep the table plain.

story buttermark [topic=food|memories]
  : A drop of butter made a perfect bright circle on a lid. I polished round it before noticing the trouble.
  : The butter was a reflection from the dish beside me.
  b : Did you finish polishing?
  : Yes. One corner of that lid has never been so needlessly clean.

story tinrain [topic=weather|memories]
  : I took a cover onto a dry sill to cool and heard what might have been the first few raindrops.
  : The sky was clear. A wet hem I'd hung above it was doing an excellent imitation.
  b : How long did it rain?
  : Just as long as it took me to move the cover. Very local weather.

rule @rim
when concept=bark
does aside
cooldown 8h
say Turn the rim away before you lift. | Let that last bead drop back.

rule @pot
when concept=bark working=yes self.job=servant
does aside
cooldown 8h
say Dry cloth for the hot cover, please. | Keep the loose rings from knocking on the tray.

rule @mist
when concept=bark here.weather=fog
does aside
cooldown 8h
say The spout's tip has almost vanished through this grey. | Mist outside and steam within. I'm between them.

rule @pause
when concept=bark
does aside
cooldown 8h
say Let me hear whether that ring settles. | Better set down than left balanced on an edge.

dlg @1 resident.hub : I can leave this covered while I hear what brings you.
dlg @2 resident.hub [topic.meeting=known] : #topic.player#, I've kept a quiet corner free.
dlg @3 resident.hub [here.time=night] : A low voice will carry far enough. The clatter's died down.
dlg @4 resident.hub [pair.disposition=wary|hostile] : Stay in sight and leave my things where they are, please.
dlg @1 resident.job [self.job=servant] : #self.trade_words.capitalize#. Every dish has its own convenient time for taking the cover off.
dlg @2 resident.job : I try to leave things quiet, clean and ready for whoever follows.
dlg @1 resident.bye : May your roof keep its promises.
graft resident.hub
choice What does the ring on a serving cover tell you? -> coverring
node coverring
say If it rattles against the tin I've tilted too far for carrying. That's a remarkably useful little warning for something that wasn't made to give one.
free
choice Do you ever still the ring? -> stillring
choice I can hear it tapping now. -> hub
node stillring
say After setting down, certainly. Everything that might topple is now at rest. The ring is quite entitled to rest with it.
choice I'll leave the cover alone. -> hub
choice Time to take my leave. -> bye
